# Root-level data downloads / dumps (transient — never commit)
/*.zip
# NO TRAILING SLASH — a slashed pattern matches DIRECTORIES ONLY, so it silently fails on the case it
# most needs to catch: a data root that is a SYMLINK. Exactly the trap already recorded further up
# this file for subprojects/Parametric-Indicators/data ("on the server this path is a SYMLINK"), and
# it recurred verbatim when the legacy18 worktree symlinked these three back to the main checkout —
# `/data/` ignored the real directory in the parent and missed the symlink in the worktree.
# These are price-data roots. They must never be committed whether they are directories or links.
/data
/ALL_STOCKS
/Full_Canldes_Data

